the original root","Plan does not enumerate a restore/reset path for the runner root after a files-case completes"],"finding":"The eval-solver change reroots the injected runner into a per-case disposable repository, but the plan does not state that the reroot is scoped to the case and restored/reset afterward. If the runner instance is reused across eval cases, a rerooted runner could leak the disposable repository root into a subsequent case that lacks `files` and runs on the inline path, corrupting its execution context.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffcbf5832f7f28298","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet: 'When a case supplies `files`, create the existing disposable case repository, reroot the injected runner there, then execute the code-review prompt against the inline diff.'","norm_id":"n771fd2b9e65ec5f5","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A files-case reroots the runner into its disposable repo; a following no-files inline case inherits the stale root and resolves paths against the wrong repository, producing a wrong or empty result."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State in the eval-solver step that the reroot is applied to a per-case runner copy (or is reset in a finally block) so subsequent inline cases retain the original root.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that for `files` cases the disposable fixture root is threaded as `repo_root` into BOTH prompt resolution and the rerooted runner, so read root and prompt context agree.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'reroot the injected runner there, then execute the code-review prompt against the inline diff' — names only the runner reroot","eval_solver.py:228-234 `_run_code_review_case` passes `repo_root=repo_root` into `prompts.get_prompt` and `resolve_prompt_cached`","eval_solver.py:271-277 `_rerooted` rebuilds only the runner's `cfg.repo_path`/`tickets_path`"],"finding":"The eval-solver extension names rerooting the injected runner to the disposable fixture but does not state that the fixture root must also be threaded as `repo_root` into prompt resolution; `_run_code_review_case` currently resolves the prompt via `prompts.get_prompt(prompt_id, repo_root=repo_root)` and `resolve_prompt_cached(..., repo_root=repo_root)`. If only the runner is rerooted while prompt resolution keeps the original eval-checkout root, the agent's read root and the prompt-context root can diverge for `files` cases.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f26be65458c213dd9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step: 'Extend the code-review arm in src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py'","norm_id":"neb2fb3553e9ed19c","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A `files` fire case runs agentically but the prompt was resolved against the eval checkout root, so repo-relative context/tools disagree and the case fails or mis-fires